abstract: >-
  A dictionary-first harmonisation tool for aligning constructs across five longitudinal
  youth-development cohorts (LSAC, ABCD, TESS, Ten to Men and LSIC) without access
  to participant data. It produces a construct coverage matrix, a register of constructs
  declared non-harmonisable with reasons, an assessment of whether pooled latent modelling
  is feasible for each cohort pair, and an audit of published methodological claims against
  the cohorts' own dictionaries. Governed cohorts are gated in code rather than in prose.
